  "problem": "Construct an integral that represents the area of this circle using rectangular coordinates.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{0}^{6}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\,\\,\\text{d}x$",
  "worked_solution": "Since  $y=\\sqrt{6x-{x}^{2}}$ represents the upper semicircle  and  $y=-\\sqrt{6x-{x}^{2}}$ represents the lower semicircle, the area $A$ of the circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}[(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}[(\\sqrt{6x-{x}^{2}})-(-\\sqrt{6x-{x}^{2}})]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}2\\sqrt{6x-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
